    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.starter\n\n### Description\n\nProblem: The text in the starter screen is all the same color.\r\nSolution: A method that we could call to color content for the screen. It would take in a string and output the colored text, as for which colors specifically I don't know, ideally it would take in any color, but realistically if we were able to pick from a set of them (out of mini's theme) it would be equally great.",
